Z||000017||mwbackus||04-12-2000||11:33 AM||||I am glad you are sticking around Stimpy!  Its not easy to make friends on an Internet forum, and you have obviously been quite successful at this.  <P>Many people would love it if I left the forum.  I post when I have significant knowlegde on a subject to be of some assistance, and I will usually correct inaccurate statements for the sack of clarity. I am sure that this offends many of the posters here, but I feel it is more important than a few bruised feelings.  Many "lurkers" use this as a research tool rather than just a discuusion forum, and IMO the information needs to be as correct as possible.  <P>Believe it or not, I have no ill feelings towards anyone on this forum, and even those that have proven their word to be completely worthless in some of my own business dealings, still have a right to their opinion.  Although I would promptly point out my own experience if I see these flakes trying to take advantage of anyone else on the forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I guess what I am trying to say is that IMO the Internet has become a vehicle for some to hide behind, writing things from the comfort and distance of their modems that they would never have the guts to say to your face.  They are on the same level as the guy who nearly runs into you as he cuts you off without a signal in trafic, then proceeds to flip you off from the safety of his car as he quickly makes his "getaway" turn, knowing that you are unlikly to catch him for a "face to face" evaluation of his actions.  Its really to bad that so many good folks have to deal with these mental midgets, AFTER, we get home from our daily commutes.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fieroshop||04-12-2000||10:38 PM||||Hey Stimpy, glad you decided to stick around. I mean besides a few other people on the forum you have had personal dealings with me and my shop and you have recomended my shop to several people and I really appreciate it very much. I can use all the help I can get. If I can get my son off his lazy butt I'll have my online parts catalog soon. I hope. I just e-mailed him asking him to please finish it and get it up and running.||||reg||6
Z||000019||stimpy||04-13-2000||07:51 AM||||Well, if anyone is curious about what <BR>this had been all about, a certain <BR>forum member has regurgitated this <BR>whole mess up from his hard drive, <BR>for philanthropic reasons to be sure.<BR> Personally, I don't see what educational comments are included, and it does leave out the post that the originator of the first thread left at the end of the second thread that it was all a joke. Not that it makes any difference.<BR>The whole thing makes me sad.<BR>I wish it would go away and stay away.||||reg||1
